Build the Docker image
-> docker build -f docker/Dockerfile.flink --no-cache -t pyflink:latest .
Remove old container
->docker rm pyflink-container
Run the container interactively
->docker run -it --name pyflink-container pyflink:latest /bin/bash
Mount host jobs folder to container
->docker run -it -v ${PWD}/jobs:/app/jobs pyflink:latest /bin/bash   # this create a new container using flink imag
->docker exec -it pyflink /bin/bash

Run Flink jobs
->python3 /app/jobs/flink_consumer.py
